  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>The European University of Lisbon (Universidade Europeia) is one of Portugal’s most internationally oriented private universities. The university focuses on preparing you for real-world careers through its courses in design, business, technology, tourism, and social sciences.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>Life at Universidade Europeia is vibrant and multicultural, since more than 30% of the students are international. You can participate in clubs, associations, and extracurricular projects, while the university offers support for international students like you, with Welcome Week activities.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>Universidade Europeia doesn’t offer on-campus residences, but it partners with several modern student housing providers around Lisbon.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>You’ll get access to libraries across campuses, plus extensive online databases, study rooms, and research support staff.</p><p><strong>Laboratory</strong><br>At Universidade Europeia, you’ll find various specialised labs, including the Dissection Laboratory for health sciences at its Madrid campus and the Fábrica at its IADE campus in Lisbon.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
